to think things through,

318
00:16:54,138 --> 00:16:55,848
so I didn't request a date.

319
00:16:55,931 --> 00:16:57,474
- I see.
- He wanted to give her time.

320
00:16:57,558 --> 00:16:58,767
He didn't want to pressure her.

321
00:17:00,019 --> 00:17:00,936
He's so…

322
00:17:01,437 --> 00:17:03,772
He's so "unrude."

323
00:17:03,856 --> 00:17:04,940
He's the opposite of rude.

324
00:17:05,024 --> 00:17:07,067
- Oh, he's the opposite?
- Yeah.

325
00:17:07,151 --> 00:17:08,819
- He's "unrude."
- Unlike Tae-hoon, who is rude.

326
00:17:08,902 --> 00:17:10,946
- He's respectful.
- He is.

327
00:17:11,030 --> 00:17:12,239
- He lacks rudeness.
- He's "unrude."

328
00:17:12,322 --> 00:17:15,034
He's a ball of good manners.
He's super courteous.

329
00:17:15,117 --> 00:17:16,201
- Yes.
- He's "unrude."

330
00:17:16,785 --> 00:17:17,911
- Do you think it's cooked?
- Yes.

331
00:17:17,995 --> 00:17:18,996
- Here you go.
- Let's eat.

332
00:17:19,079 --> 00:17:20,122
Thank you.

333
00:17:20,748 --> 00:17:21,874
Oh my.

334
00:17:23,459 --> 00:17:26,295
- He gave her the first piece.
- That's not an easy thing to do.

335
00:17:27,296 --> 00:17:28,380
It looks so tasty.

336
00:17:29,339 --> 00:17:30,716
Go ahead and eat first.

337
00:17:30,799 --> 00:17:32,176
No, let's eat together.

338
00:17:32,760 --> 00:17:34,303
Together? Right, we should do that.

339
00:17:38,932 --> 00:17:41,727
Have you organized your thoughts?

340
00:17:42,311 --> 00:17:44,104
Even until this morning--

341
00:17:44,188 --> 00:17:45,689
- You're not sure?
- Yeah, I was in my room

342
00:17:45,773 --> 00:17:46,982
